---
layout: null
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  The list of pages offered to a search engine, derived from the site itself so
  it cannot fall out of step. Never maintain this by hand.

  Three exclusions, all deliberate and all visible here rather than hidden in a
  page's front matter:
    - the 404, which should never be indexed
    - anything that sets `sitemap: false`, including this file and the feed
    - a filter page with nothing on it — offering an empty page to a search
      engine invites it to be classified as a soft 404

  The item count is derived from the page's own front matter, so a term that
  gains its first item appears here on the next build, and one that loses its
  last drops out. There is no list of terms to maintain.

  Every address uses absolute_url, so it names crissouza.org and matches that
  page's canonical exactly.
{%- endcomment -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- for page in site.pages %}
{%- assign items = -1 -%}
{%- if page.type -%}
  {%- assign matched = site.data.bookmarks | where: 'type', page.type -%}
  {%- assign items = matched.size -%}
{%- elsif page.keyword -%}
  {%- assign matched = site.posts | where_exp: 'p', 'p.keywords contains page.keyword' -%}
  {%- assign items = matched.size -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- unless page.sitemap == false or page.url contains '404' or page.url contains '.xml' or page.url contains '.txt' or items == 0 %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ page.url | absolute_url }}</loc>
  </url>
{%- endunless %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for post in site.posts %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ post.url | absolute_url }}</loc>
    <lastmod>{{ post.date | date_to_xmlschema }}</lastmod>
  </url>
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
